    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d543">

                <pb facs="0746" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg734"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/9–446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Political Adviser in Korea</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Langdon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1946-09-04T13:53:00+09:00"
                            notBefore="1946-08-31T17:30:00+09:00">undated</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        September 4—1:53 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Tfpol 30 [to Tokyo]. 103. Timing and text of Under Secretary’s statement
                    following immediately upon General Hodge’s statement <pb facs="0747" n="735"
                        xml:id="pg735"/> here<anchor n="46" xml:id="d543-f1"/> was eminently
                    effective. All Korean papers from extreme Eight to extreme Left and Korean news
                    services carried full layout UP Washington coverage and enthusiastically
                    received by Korean people. Such frank and definitive statement of policy at
                    State Dept level believed to be of great assistance stabilizing and
                    crystallizing future Korean political activities. High level emphasis to
                    previous statements by Hodge most helpful. Further, statement gave army
                    personnel here boost in appreciation of occupational tasks. Hodge grateful for
                    assistance and hopes in future Dept will issue similar statements of high level
                    policy as need develops.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Langdon</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d543-f1" n="46" xml:id="d543-f1-content">
                <p>The text of General Hodge’s statement was transmitted by telegram on August 31
                    from Seoul; received at 5:30 p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
